{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The tents of</b> — the meaning is Edom. In their tents, or they dwelt [in] the tents of Edom because they joined themselves to them, and they are the principal ones; and likewise the inhabitants of Tyre." "<b>And the Hagrites</b> — they are the Hagrites whom Hagar bore from another husband, and because she was Abraham's maidservant, the children were traced to her, in the manner of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 83, :notes {0 "The syntax of Ibn Ezra's first two phrases is compressed; I read 'the meaning is Edom' as his gloss on the lemma, and the two alternatives (באהליהם / שכנו) as parsing options for the construct."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:55.191401638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}